## Generated client assets.
##
## NOTE what is NOT here: src/Crm04.Web/wwwroot/css/app.css. It is generated, and it is
## COMMITTED anyway, because the plant server has neither Node nor internet and can never
## rebuild it. It WAS ignored, while Crm04.Web.csproj claimed the opposite - so a ZIP of this
## repo reached production with no stylesheet at all, npm was absent, and the dashboard
## rendered completely unstyled behind nothing but an MSB3073 warning.
##
## Crm04.Web.csproj now fails the build if that file is missing. Rebuild it
## (cd src/Crm04.Web/ClientApp && npm run build:css) in the SAME commit as any change to
## Styles/app.css or to a .razor file that uses a new Tailwind class.
src/Crm04.Web/ClientApp/node_modules/

## Nothing produces or references these bundles any more - kept only so a stray local file
## from an older build is not accidentally committed.
src/Crm04.Web/wwwroot/js/twin.bundle.js
src/Crm04.Web/wwwroot/js/twin.bundle.js.map
src/Crm04.Web/wwwroot/js/charts.bundle.js
src/Crm04.Web/wwwroot/js/charts.bundle.js.map

## Generated replay data (produced by scripts/exportSimFrames.ts).
## Large and reproducible - regenerate rather than commit.
data/replay/*.jsonl
data/replay/*.csv

## Generated seed SQL (produced from src/data/tagDefinitions.ts).
## Regenerated so it cannot drift from the TypeScript catalogue.
db/seed/tag_definitions.sql

## Local secrets - the Oracle connection string lives in user-secrets or an env var,
## never in appsettings.json.
appsettings.Local.json
*.env
